User: Here are the raw notes from our 45-minute Q3 Roadmap & Infrastructure sync. Please synthesize them into an executive meeting summary:
"Attendees: Sarah (VP Eng), Mike (Principal Architect), Lisa (Product Lead), Jordan (DevOps).
Discussed migrating from Kubernetes on-prem to Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE). Mike noted on-prem hardware is approaching end-of-life in December. Sarah asked about budget. Jordan estimated GKE managed nodes will save 20% in maintenance hours, but network egress might increase by $2k/mo. Decided to proceed with GKE migration for non-production environments first by Nov 15. Lisa raised concern about developer onboarding. Decided Jordan will run two 1-hour workshop sessions in late October. Open question: whether to use Autopilot or Standard cluster mode. Mike to conduct benchmark test by next Friday."
Assistant: # Executive Meeting Summary: Q3 Roadmap & Infrastructure Sync

**Date:** September 9, 2026  
**Participants:** Sarah (VP Eng), Mike (Principal Architect), Lisa (Product Lead), Jordan (DevOps)  
**Topic:** Infrastructure Modernization: GKE Migration Strategy  

---

## Executive Summary
The engineering leadership team approved initiating Phase 1 migration from on-prem Kubernetes to Google Kubernetes Engine (GKE) for non-production environments by November 15, mitigating hardware end-of-life risks in December.

## Key Decisions Made
1. **Approved Non-Prod GKE Migration:** Non-production workloads will migrate to GKE by November 15, 2026.
2. **Developer Enablement:** DevOps will conduct two 1-hour training workshops in late October to onboard engineering teams.

## Discussion Highlights & Financial Analysis
- **Hardware Lifecycle:** On-premise infrastructure reaches mandatory end-of-life in December 2026.
- **Cost & Efficiency Trade-offs:** GKE reduces ongoing maintenance by an estimated 20% in engineer hours, offset by ~$2,000/month in projected network egress.

## Open Questions & Risks
- **Cluster Operational Mode:** Evaluating GKE Autopilot vs. Standard mode regarding custom kernel tuning requirements.

## Action Items & Ownership
- **DRI: Mike (Principal Architect)** — Benchmark GKE Autopilot vs. Standard mode and deliver recommendation memo by **Friday, September 18**.
- **DRI: Jordan (DevOps)** — Provision non-production GKE staging environment by **October 15**.
- **DRI: Jordan (DevOps) / Lisa (Product)** — Schedule developer onboarding workshops for **late October**.

